Here are the best JVM options for Spring Cloud Gateway with WebMVC to avoid memory leaks:

## Essential Memory Configuration

```bash
# Heap Size (adjust based on your needs)
-Xms2g                          # Initial heap size
-Xmx2g                          # Maximum heap size (same as Xms for consistency)

# Metaspace (for class metadata)
-XX:MetaspaceSize=256m
-XX:MaxMetaspaceSize=512m       # Prevents metaspace from growing indefinitely
```

## Garbage Collection Options

### For Java 11+ (Recommended: G1GC)
```bash
-XX:+UseG1GC                    # Use G1 garbage collector
-XX:MaxGCPauseMillis=200        # Target max GC pause time
-XX:G1HeapRegionSize=16m        # Region size for G1
-XX:+ParallelRefProcEnabled     # Parallel reference processing
-XX:InitiatingHeapOccupancyPercent=45  # Start concurrent cycle earlier
```

### For Java 17+ (Alternative: ZGC for low latency)
```bash
-XX:+UseZGC                     # Ultra-low latency GC
-XX:ZCollectionInterval=5       # Collection interval in seconds
```

## Memory Leak Detection & Prevention

```bash
